// Contract-only records (proposal section 4, rule G; NEXT.md entry 13).
//
// A matrix names the units of a machine of the same stem. A matrix with no
// machine is legal only as a contract-only record: an immutable or
// creation-time record whose ARCHITECTURE.md persistence-and-placement row
// waives the machine with '(no machine: <reason>)'. The waiver is the
// declaration; G3 and Gd read the same waiver (gates.NoMachineWaivers), so a
// waived matrix is neither a G3 orphan nor a Gd missing owner.
//
// finding_orphan_matrix: a matrix with neither a machine nor a waiver (a
// stale artifact, or a record whose placement row forgot the waiver).
//
// finding_waived_machine_present: a waiver on a component that has a
// machine. The waiver says there is no lifecycle and the machine says there
// is one; one of the two statements is stale.

.decl matrix(id:symbol)
.input matrix
.decl machine(id:symbol)
.input machine
.decl no_machine_waiver(component:symbol)
.input no_machine_waiver

.decl finding_orphan_matrix(matrix:symbol)
.output finding_orphan_matrix
finding_orphan_matrix(M) :- matrix(M), !machine(M), !no_machine_waiver(M).

.decl finding_waived_machine_present(component:symbol)
.output finding_waived_machine_present
finding_waived_machine_present(C) :- no_machine_waiver(C), machine(C).
